{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889289-werewolf-pack-in-a-crossover-game","id":889289,"title":"Werewolf Pack in a Crossover Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T12:29:33-07:00","id":889289,"title":"Werewolf Pack in a Crossover Game","content":"I'm probably going to be playing a Werewolf in a crossover game in the near future, and I'm wondering how one might handle pack creation in such a chronicle in which only one player was a werewolf? I know The Pack goes into detail about adding in other supernaturals, but from the start, I'm fairly certain the ST wants to have my character already be part of a pack. I had thought simply to think up 'NPC' Uratha that are the other werewolves, since the Totem would be rather inefficient given the low number of Totem Merit points with just one Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:45:43-07:00","id":889296,"title":"","content":"You could have two wolf blooded npcs as your pack mates with each contributing 1 to the totem. That way your st doesn't have to worry about the power of werewolf npcs. If you include the other supernaturals in your pack they can contribute and benifit as well.<br /> <br /> It still won't be too efficient for the rewards from the totem but it would allow the totem to be stronger fir cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:51:55-07:00","id":889301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889289-werewolf-pack-in-a-crossover-game?p=889296#post889296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have two wolf blooded npcs as your pack mates with each contributing 1 to the totem. That way your st doesn't have to worry about the power of werewolf npcs. If you include the other supernaturals in your pack they can contribute and benifit as well.<br /> <br /> It still won't be too efficient for the rewards from the totem but it would allow the totem to be stronger fir cheaper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was something I considered after my initial thought, yeah. Likely, one or two of the other supernaturals will join the Pack, but initially they'll have their own things to worry about. I suppose it could be interesting from a narrative standpoint to have the Totem grow as it accepts in, say, a Changeling or a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:57:08-07:00","id":889304,"title":"","content":"Oh ya, I'd just suggest to try and build your totem with that in mind as a possibility but it as you said would be unlikely to be how it'd start.<br /> <br /> Just remember that the totem is itself it's own benifit like a retainer in a way but with added benifits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T18:07:24-07:00","id":889514,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing from the Pack I've noticed is the idea that Lone Wolves will often join Spirit Broods if they can't find fellow Werewolves to join up with. So its probably pretty spot on for your Werewolf to create a pack with Wolf-Blooded, Mortals, and Spirits joining in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T20:19:48-07:00","id":889588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889289-werewolf-pack-in-a-crossover-game?p=889514#post889514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing from the Pack I've noticed is the idea that Lone Wolves will often join Spirit Broods if they can't find fellow Werewolves to join up with. So its probably pretty spot on for your Werewolf to create a pack with Wolf-Blooded, Mortals, and Spirits joining in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now I have to pick up the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:04:22-07:00","id":889652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889289-werewolf-pack-in-a-crossover-game?p=889588#post889588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, now I have to pick up the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also consider indicting the other players into the pack. And work towards the Magnaninous Totem Pack merit (pg. 30). It would allow you to let other characters spend more dots on the totem merit. Let the other players get the benefit of being in a pack, and let you have a stronger totem. <br /> <br /> Also side note pack experience lets you improve the secondary characters in the pack (pg. 20). So you can also use the pack exp to put more dots in totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:17:43-07:00","id":889656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889289-werewolf-pack-in-a-crossover-game?p=889652#post889652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also consider indicting the other players into the pack. And work towards the Magnaninous Totem Pack merit (pg. 30). It would allow you to let other characters spend more dots on the totem merit. Let the other players get the benefit of being in a pack, and let you have a stronger totem. <br /> <br /> Also side note pack experience lets you improve the secondary characters in the pack (pg. 20). So you can also use the pack exp to put more dots in totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I thought the reward was the same for everyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:30:21-07:00","id":889662,"title":"","content":"The reward is the same. <br /> I'm just saying that with letting the other players inthe pack. along with the merit mentioned above. (Which by the way lets none werewolves spend more the 1exp on totem). <br /> It would allow starkjunior to spend less of his own exp to boost the totem sense im assuming the other party members would want to spend exp to boost everybody in the pack. So the cost is spread out more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:51:35-07:00","id":889705,"title":"","content":"Ah, understood. Encourage all to pay an equal price for the same reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}